# #5837, the forward-exclusion relief (a5e2e2ef's X1-X4).
MODULE: ForwardHonestForwardExclusionByInMemorySpan
TARGET: ForwardHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a reader excludes on its in-memory narrow, persisted or not: a stale duplicate whose persist lost passes its own forward of a key L still owns (X3)
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithFwdExclusion = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE

--- FIND
FwdExcluded(a, o) == Persisted(a) /\ fTag[o] = nar[a]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the reader's in-memory span.
FwdExcluded(a, o) == nar[a] # NoTag /\ fTag[o] = nar[a]
--- END
